course: dictionary
lesson: 15293
title: Skateboarder
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be built from smaller parts. Skateboarder is made from skate, board and -er. The ending -er often means a person who does something, so a skateboarder is a person who skateboards. «The skateboarder rolled down the ramp and landed a perfect ollie.» Ramp and landed tell you the skateboarder is riding a board.
explain: Context clues also show you where skateboarders are. «Skateboarders at the skate park cheered when Mia landed her kickflip.» A skate park is a place built for skateboarding, so the clue skate park tells you what a skateboarder does there.
explain: Safety words in a text help you learn too. «Many skateboarders wear a helmet and pads to stay safe.» Helmet and pads are protection, so this sentence tells you that skateboarding can be risky and that careful people protect themselves.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try: «The person who rides a skateboard rolled down the ramp.» It still makes sense, so skateboarder means a person who rides a skateboard.
fact: A skateboarder is a person who rides a skateboard.
fact: A skateboard is a short board on four small wheels.
fact: Skateboarders often do tricks, such as an ollie or a kickflip.
fact: Skateboarders usually ride in skate parks, on ramps or on pavements, and safety lessons say to wear a helmet and pads.
fact: Skateboarding has been an Olympic sport since 2021, and some Olympic skateboarders were children.
exercise: «The skateboarder rode up the ramp and flew through the air.» What is a skateboarder? | A type of bicycle with four wheels | A small truck that carries boards to the park | A teacher who works at a skate park | *A person who rides a skateboard, often doing tricks
exercise: Ella says a skateboarder must ride on busy roads to be brave. What do safety lessons say? | Skate only at night when it is dark | Ride as fast as you can on busy roads | *Wear a helmet and pads, and do not ride on busy roads | Never wear a helmet, because it looks silly
exercise: «Jay landed a clean ollie at the skate park.» Find and copy one word that is the name of a trick. | *ollie | park | skate | Jay
test: «Skateboarders at the skate park cheered when Mia landed her kickflip.» Where do skateboarders often ride? | Inside a library | *In skate parks, on ramps and on pavements | Under the sea | On the moon
test: The word skateboarder ends in -er. What does the ending -er often mean? | A place to sleep | A thing that is broken | *A person who does something | A word for a colour
exam: «Many skateboarders wear a helmet and pads to stay safe.» What does this sentence tell you about skateboarding? | *It can be risky, so riders protect themselves | It is a sport for birds | It is always completely safe, so no protection is needed | It is only for adults
